                                            defined as p < 0.05. To facilitate correlation analysis, the metal concentrations below the detection limits (detec-
                                            tion limits for Cu, Zn, Pb, Cd, Fe, and Mn were 0.005, 0.005, 0.03, 0.002, 0.002, and 0.0005 mg ­L−1, respectively)
                                            were replaced with a half of the detection limit value, and this could not affect the conclusions. Furthermore, to
