docs/schema-history.md:13:| 2026-05-08 | + tAs, U | Extended to current 10-metal set. tAs added as a separate sub-block from iAs because most occurrence surveys report total arsenic and the iAs/tAs split is non-negotiable. U added because the wiki's scope is "heavy metals in food" rather than "HMTc-certified analytes" and uranium is a recognized toxic heavy metal of rising public-health attention even though not in the HMTc-10 analyte vocabulary. |
docs/schema-history.md:22:The `last_full_resynthesis` field was formerly carried per-metal-sub-block on ingredient pages. As of 2026-05, resynthesis events are tracked in the structured-evidence layer at `data/evidence/review_events.jsonl`, which is authoritative. CLAUDE.md Part 9's conceptual logic (when to trigger full resynthesis vs incremental update) still applies; only the implementation has moved off the page frontmatter.
docs/schemas/index.md:52:Every migration script under `tools/migrate-*.mjs` writes one row per touched page to `data/evidence/migrations/<migration>-<date>.csv`. The audit trail is meant to be re-readable years later without git archaeology.
docs/schemas/index.md:56:- `tools/migrate-future-slots.mjs` — adds `wiki_doi`, and (on source pages only) `sampling_locations`, `sampling_year_range`. Idempotent. Audit at `data/evidence/migrations/future-slots-<date>.csv`.
docs/schemas/source-page.md:9:Source pages document one paper / agency report / dataset each. They are the atomic evidence units; every public wiki claim traces to one or more of these via the routing audit (`data/evidence/product_source_routing_audit.csv`).
docs/gpt-collaboration/README.md:22:  - **Default (autonomous, Karen out of loop):** the `ingest-next-manual-fetch-pdf` skill spawns a Claude subagent via the Agent tool after each ingest commit. The subagent reads the page + source, runs the five checks, returns the structured report. Main Claude verifies findings independently, applies real ones, pushes back on false positives, commits, updates `data/evidence/audit-queue.csv`. No Karen interaction needed.
docs/gpt-collaboration/audit-prompt.md:118:Note: the `## Implications` section is allowed to describe what the paper's findings contribute to threshold work, but must not propose threshold values. The boundary is between "contributes occurrence data for product category X" (allowed) and "suggests HMTc should certify at Y ppb" (not allowed).
