wiki/sources/arsenic2025-unknown.md:81:Sample digestion: 1.0 g rice + 10 mL 0.2 % (v/v) HNO₃, two 5 mL aliquots, vortex, heat-block 90 °C × 1 h 30 min, cool, centrifuge 4000 rpm × 30 min, supernatant + 9 mL mobile phase, 0.22 µm + 0.45 µm filtration, first mL discarded. Calibration 0.25-20.0 µg/L, R² ≥ 0.999. LOD 0.114-0.398 µg/kg, LOQ 0.345-1.207 µg/kg. CRM SRM 1568b Rice Flour recovery 74.5-108.6 % at three spike levels (3, 8, 15 µg/L); within ICH 70-120 % acceptance range. MMA excluded due to anomalous recoveries (405-453 %, attributed to matrix interferences). Total arsenic was estimated as the sum of measured species (AsIII + AsV + DMA), not via separate total-As digestion.

